WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.050
The standard is short on purpose.

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:07.158
It says what has to be true for any
partner, on any platform, in nine areas:

3
00:00:07.158 --> 00:00:12.618
partner qualification, trust establishment,
population scope, assurance,

4
00:00:12.618 --> 00:00:17.638
authorization, lifecycle, data
protection, operations and evidence.

5
00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:21.224
Each area becomes a section of
the partner identity record.

6
00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:23.600
Three points matter most to leadership.

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.652
Authorization is separate from authentication:
a valid sign-in at the state proves

8
00:00:28.652 --> 00:00:33.338
the examiner signed in there; only an
agency assignment opens the case system.

9
00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:37.315
Partner exit is a lifecycle
event: when an agreement ends,

10
00:00:37.315 --> 00:00:40.362
the accounts are removed,
not left disabled.

11
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:45.546
And statements are not controls: a
partner saying it requires MFA is input

12
00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:50.950
to the agreement, while a policy the
agency enforces and tests is the control.
